<section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">A SIMPLE PROCESS</p><h1>From lost to found.</h1><p class="lead">Use the same clear process whether you lost an item or found something on campus.</p></section>
<section class="steps-grid"><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">1</span><h2>Create a report</h2><p>Sign in and choose <strong>Report lost</strong> or <strong>Report found</strong>. Add a clear description, category, date, location and an optional photo.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">2</span><h2>Search and match</h2><p>Browse current reports. The system can flag similar lost and found entries and notify signed-in users when a possible match appears.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">3</span><h2>Submit a claim</h2><p>Describe identifying details that are not public. Never post passwords, full card numbers, or sensitive personal information.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">4</span><h2>Verify and return</h2><p>Follow the claim status and coordinate a safe handover after ownership has been verified by the responsible campus team.</p></article></section>
<section class="callout"><h2>Ready to look for your item?</h2><p>Start with a keyword or browse all active reports.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/search">Search reports</a><a class="btn btn-lost" href="/report/lost">Report a lost item</a><a class="btn btn-found" href="/report/found">Report a found item</a></div></section>
